      "stem": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "A family farm has two fields. The north field is divided into 7 equal sections, with k acres of crops planted in each section. The south field is divided into 3 equal sections, also with k acres of crops planted in each section, plus an additional 20 acres planted along its border fence. If the total number of acres planted in the north field equals the total number of acres planted in the south field, what is the value of k?"
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "accept": [
          "5"
        ],
        "tol": 0
      },
      "solution": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "1. isolate variable: Translate the context into an equation: north field total = 7k; south field total = 3k + 20. Setting them equal gives 7k = 3k + 20."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "2. subtract constant: Subtract 3k from both sides to collect the variable term on one side: 7k − 3k = 3k + 20 − 3k, which simplifies to 4k = 20."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "3. divide coefficient: Divide both sides by the combined coefficient 4: k = 20 ÷ 4 = 5. Since 5 is a positive integer, the answer is reasonable in context (whole-number acres per section)."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        }
      ],
