      "stem": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "At a farmers market, a vendor prices fresh peaches at r dollars per pound. A customer purchases 5 pounds of peaches and pays a flat $3 packaging fee, for a total cost of $19. The equation below represents this situation.\n\n5r + 3 = 19\n\nWhat is the value of r?"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "4/5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "16/5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "19/5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "22/5"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "correct": "B"
      },
      "solution": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "1. subtract constant: Subtract 3 from both sides of 5r + 3 = 19 to isolate the variable term: 5r + 3 − 3 = 19 − 3, which gives 5r = 16."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "2. divide coefficient: Divide both sides by 5: r = 16/5. Because GCD(16, 5) = 1, the fraction is already fully reduced. Since 5 does not divide 16 evenly, the answer is a non-integer fraction, not a whole number."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        }
      ],
