      "stem": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Two players in a retro video game tournament finish a round with the same high score. Player 1's score, in thousands of points, is 3h + 5, and Player 2's score is h/2 + 20, where h is the number of bonus stages each player completed. What is the value of h?"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "10"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "15"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "correct": "B"
      },
      "solution": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "1. move variable term: Set the two expressions equal to form 3h + 5 = h/2 + 20. Subtract h/2 from both sides and subtract 5 from both sides simultaneously to collect variable terms on the left and constants on the right: 3h − h/2 = 20 − 5. Rewrite 3h as 6h/2 and combine: (6h/2 − h/2) = 15, giving (5/2)h = 15."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "2. divide coefficient: Divide both sides by the net fractional coefficient 5/2, which is equivalent to multiplying both sides by 2/5: h = 15 × (2/5) = 30/5 = 6."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        }
      ],
